      "item": {
        "type": "agentMessage",
        "id": "msg_0852b2876f12cbb7016acbaefc6cf087d09167dd36dc3954b3",
        "text": "Service A accepts reservation requests; Service B owns the inventory ledger. Each request carries a unique idempotency key.\n\nB atomically creates a time-limited hold only if inventory is available, recording the key so retries return the same reservation. A requests payment using that key. B confirms the reservation only if payment succeeds before the hold expires.\n\nDuring a partition, allowing both services to grant reservations could allocate the same inventory twice. Requiring B\u2019s approval prevents duplicates but makes new reservations unavailable when B cannot be reached.\n\nChoose consistency: A returns \u201cpending\u201d during a partition and never promises inventory without B\u2019s approval.\n\nRecovery rule: reconcile payment results against B\u2019s ledger; refund any successful payment whose hold expired, and never revive an expired hold automatically.",
        "phase": "final_answer",
        "memoryCitation": null,
        "delivery": null,
        "questions": null
      }
    },
