        "text": "Service A handles requests and payment; Service B owns inventory. Each request has a unique idempotency key.\n\nB atomically creates a time-limited hold if inventory is available. Retries with the same key return the same hold. Payment confirmation converts an active hold into a reservation.\n\nDuring a network partition, letting both services allocate inventory independently risks duplicate reservations. Requiring B\u2019s approval prevents duplicates but makes new reservations unavailable when B cannot be reached.\n\nChoose consistency: A returns \u201cpending\u201d during partitions and promises inventory only after B approves.\n\nRecovery rule: after connectivity returns, reconcile payments against B\u2019s ledger. Refund successful payments for expired holds; never automatically revive an expired hold.",
